<title>BRAZIL: Brazil may ask Paraguay to help on state debt scam.</title>
<headline>Brazil may ask Paraguay to help on state debt scam.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank is studying whether to ask the Paraguayan Central Bank to cooperate in tracking down the illicit profits made in a spiralling multi-million dollar municipal bond scam, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the bank was considering whether to approach authorities in neighbouring Paraguay in conjunction with a probe launched by the Brazilian Senate.</p>
<p>&quot;Central Bank President Gustavo Loyola said a request for assistance from Paraguay is being studied, in conjunction with the CPI (Parliamentary Committee of Inquiry),&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
